// ============================================================================
// random_tests.cpp — the seeded PRNG must reproduce .NET CompatPrng.
//
// These expected values were captured from the real .NET 10 runtime running
// `new Random(seed)`. They are the oracle: if this test fails, the port has
// drifted from the generator the C# game logic actually uses, and every random
// gameplay decision moves. The seed set is deliberately adversarial: small,
// negative, the abs() edge cases (int.MinValue / int.MaxValue), and seeds large
// enough that the seeding's `mj` goes negative.
// ============================================================================

